  "reference_components_outperform": "plain K% beats the whole contact composite for pitchers (r=0.4906 vs composite 0.1383), and BB% does for hitters (r=0.3195 vs composite 0.1242); on the 2y-bWAR join Savant xwOBA beats the composite on both sides (hit 0.3139 vs 0.1048, pit 0.2024 vs 0.0792). The weak part of SC+ is the contact-quality framing, not the Savant source data",
  "blend_vs_composite_oos": "the forward-chained top-2 reweight is directionally positive on rate outcomes (hitters r 0.1959 vs composite 0.1211, gain 0.0748; pitchers 0.3288 vs 0.2792, gain 0.0496) but misses the pre-registered +0.05 bar on the pitcher side and REVERSES on the hitter 2y-bWAR join (blend -0.0765 vs composite 0.1421), so the reweight is not robust at these ns"
